<main id="main"><section class="pageHero"><div class="container"><span class="kicker">Infrastructure model</span><h1>Professional datacentre capacity, delivered through VPN4U.</h1><p>We operate as an independent service provider and source compute and network capacity through established infrastructure partners.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><h2>What that means for customers</h2><p>VPN4U does not claim to own every datacentre, fibre route or server chassis behind the services we sell. Instead, we select upstream infrastructure, package it into clear products, manage the customer relationship and remain your point of contact for service and support.</p><p>This model is common across hosting, connectivity and managed infrastructure markets. It gives customers access to mature datacentre platforms while dealing with one commercial provider.</p></div><div class="factPanel"><div><span>VPS platform</span><strong>NVMe virtual compute</strong><small>High-speed uplinks, snapshots and multiple global regions.</small></div><div><span>Dedicated platform</span><strong>AMD bare-metal compute</strong><small>Full root access, dedicated uplinks and European datacentres.</small></div><div><span>Connectivity</span><strong>Encrypted VPN access</strong><small>WireGuard and OpenVPN for supported plans.</small></div></div></div></section><section class="section sectionMuted"><div class="container"><div class="sectionHead"><div><span class="kicker">Operating principles</span><h2>What we commit to</h2></div></div><div class="featureGrid"><article><h3>Accurate descriptions</h3><p>We aim to describe the service actually being supplied, including resource limits, delivery model and material restrictions.</p></article><article><h3>Availability before payment</h3><p>Hardware and regional capacity can change. We confirm availability and final configuration before asking for payment.</p></article><article><h3>Responsible use</h3><p>All services are subject to our Acceptable Use Policy and applicable law. Abuse reports are reviewed through a dedicated contact channel.</p></article><article><h3>Support ownership</h3><p>Customers purchase from VPN4U and should contact VPN4U first for commercial, provisioning and support matters.</p></article></div></div></section></main>
